The RoboDojo evaluation path (the robot API, the XPolicyLab host, the motion
and perception primitives, and integrations/xpolicylab/robodojo) was split
out of that tree so it can be developed under this name. Copyright headers in
the source files are kept.

This product builds on RPent (https://github.com/RLinf/RPent),
Copyright 2026 The RPent Authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Parts kept from that line, via PyRUA-Lean, were modified:
  - src/robodojo/mcp_server.py is adapted from RPent's HttpMcpServer;
  - src/robodojo/knowledge/*.md distil operating knowledge for a program author;
  - the robot class mirrors the tool schemas (tool names, argument names and defaults).

RPent is described in: Harness VLA: Steering Frozen VLAs into Reliable
Manipulation Primitives via Memory-Guided Agents, arXiv:2607.08448
(https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.08448).
